### 1. Extend `lib/payments/process-stripe-event.ts` `handleChargeRefunded`

Currently the handler only updates `stripe_charges.status`. Extend to also mirror to `stripe_refunds` table.

The webhook event for `charge.refunded` includes `charge.refunds.data[]` array — each entry is a Stripe Refund object. Iterate and call `RPC.STRIPE_REFUND_RECORD` per entry.

Find the existing `handleChargeRefunded` function. Extend to:

```ts
async function handleChargeRefunded(
  charge: StripeChargeShape,
  supabase: SupabaseServiceClient,
): Promise<void> {
  const piId = charge.payment_intent;
  if (!piId) {
    logger.warn({ charge_id: charge.id }, 'charge.refunded: missing payment_intent — skipping');
    return;
  }

  // Update stripe_charges.status (existing behavior).
  const newStatus = charge.amount_refunded === charge.amount ? 'refunded' : 'partially_refunded';
  const fromUntyped = supabase.from.bind(supabase) as unknown as (table: string) => {
    update: (vals: Record<string, unknown>) => {
      eq: (col: string, val: string) => Promise<{ error: unknown }>;
    };
  };
  const { error: updateErr } = await fromUntyped('stripe_charges')
    .update({ status: newStatus })
    .eq('payment_intent_id', piId);
  if (updateErr) {
    logger.error({ pi_id: piId, err: updateErr }, 'charge.refunded: stripe_charges status update failed');
    throw updateErr;
  }

  // S19: mirror each refund in the charge.refunds array to stripe_refunds.
  const refunds = charge.refunds?.data ?? [];
  const studioId = charge.metadata?.inkos_studio_id ?? null;
  // Studio_id may be missing on refunds initiated outside our flow (Stripe Dashboard direct).
  // In that case, look up via stripe_charges → studio_id join.

  let resolvedStudioId = studioId;
  if (!resolvedStudioId) {
    const fromUntypedSelect = supabase.from.bind(supabase) as unknown as (table: string) => {
      select: (cols: string) => {
        eq: (col: string, val: string) => {
          maybeSingle: () => Promise<{ data: { studio_id: string } | null; error: unknown }>;
        };
      };
    };
    const { data: chargeRow } = await fromUntypedSelect('stripe_charges')
      .select('studio_id')
      .eq('payment_intent_id', piId)
      .maybeSingle();
    resolvedStudioId = chargeRow?.studio_id ?? null;
  }

  if (!resolvedStudioId) {
    logger.warn({ pi_id: piId, charge_id: charge.id }, 'charge.refunded: studio_id unresolvable — refund mirror skipped');
    return;
  }

  for (const refund of refunds) {
    const idempotencyKey = `webhook:charge.refunded:${refund.id}`;
    const { error: refundRecErr } = await supabase.rpc(RPC.STRIPE_REFUND_RECORD, {
      p_studio_id: resolvedStudioId,
      p_refund_id: refund.id,
      p_charge_id: charge.id,
      p_payment_intent_id: piId,
      p_amount_cents: refund.amount,
      p_currency: refund.currency,
      p_status: refund.status,
      p_reason: refund.reason ?? null,
      p_initiated_by_user_id: null,
      p_notes: null,
      p_metadata: refund.metadata ?? null,
      p_idempotency_key: idempotencyKey,
    });
    if (refundRecErr) {
      logger.error({ pi_id: piId, refund_id: refund.id, err: refundRecErr },
        'S19: stripe_refund_record failed — recoverable via reconciliation');
    }
  }

  logger.info({
    pi_id: piId,
    charge_id: charge.id,
    amount_refunded: charge.amount_refunded,
    refunds_mirrored: refunds.length,
    status: newStatus,
  }, 'charge.refunded webhook processed');
}
```

Extend `StripeChargeShape` interface in this file to include:
```ts
interface StripeChargeShape {
  id: string;
  payment_intent?: string | null;
  amount: number;
  amount_refunded: number;
  currency?: string | null;
  status?: string | null;
  metadata?: Record<string, string | undefined> | null;     // S19
  refunds?: { data: StripeRefundShape[] } | null;            // S19
}

interface StripeRefundShape {
  id: string;
  amount: number;
  currency: string;
  status: 'pending' | 'requires_action' | 'succeeded' | 'failed' | 'canceled';
  reason: string | null;
  metadata: Record<string, string | undefined> | null;
}
```

### 2. NEW `app/api/admin/tax-oss-export/route.ts` — POST endpoint

Admin-only EU OSS quarterly CSV export:

```
POST /api/admin/tax-oss-export

Body: { studioId: string; year: number; quarter: 1|2|3|4 }

Flow:
1. Auth check: is_platform_admin claim required.
2. Rate limit: strict (5 per minute — admin-only).
3. Validate body via Zod (year >= 2024, quarter 1-4).
4. Construct service-role supabase client.
5. Call RPC.TAX_OSS_QUARTERLY_EXPORT.
6. Generate CSV from result. Format:
   - Header row: jurisdiction, amount_collected_cents, amount_remitted_cents, amount_outstanding_cents, registration_status
   - One row per EU jurisdiction in result.jurisdictions[]
   - Footer rows: TOTAL_EU_COLLECTED, TOTAL_EU_OUTSTANDING
7. Audit log: logAuditAction({ event: 'admin_tax_oss_export', studio_id, period }).
8. Return CSV as text/csv with Content-Disposition: attachment; filename="oss-{studio_id}-{period}.csv".

On error: 500 with sanitized message.
```

Use existing admin auth pattern — check `app/api/admin/` for `requirePlatformAdmin` or similar helper. Reuse `apiRatelimit` or stricter `adminRatelimit`.

### 3. (Optional bonus) Quarterly cron `workers/cron/oss-export-quarterly.ts`

Skip for S19 — the admin endpoint is sufficient. Cron-triggered automatic export is S20+ scope.

